// load data from memory to SIMD register
// On ARM architecture, it is done by `ld1` instruction.
// `ld1` instruction has many ways to specify memory address:
// (1) [Xn|SP]
// (2) [Xn|SP], imm
// (3) [Xn|SP], Xm
// Both on ARM and on X64 architecture, this intrinsic only has one operand.
// This means it only uses one register to specify memory address.
// On LOONGARCH64 architecture, we can use `[x]vld` with `si12`==0.
